    "1099c8ed": {"text":"A fair debt can be paid by willing hands.","hash":"h1-4a0512b7"},
    "10a72829": {"text":"Courage is sometimes measured by the spoonful.","hash":"h1-a4864aeb"},
    "10aab7fb": {"text":"Turnshoe Boots","hash":"h1-c41e08fc"},
    "10ab254d": {"text":"Course after course your lance strikes true, and the field yields to you. {lord} names you champion before the assembled houses, and even the beaten men cheer.","hash":"h1-41565ac3"},
    "10b923f1": {"text":"Keys, stores, and spinning — a well-run house turns thrift into coin. (stewardship pays)","hash":"h1-8e465d17"},
    "10c07f17": {"text":"Two copies of the reeve’s seasonal tally reach your table. They agree upon every rent except the silver that should have reached your chest.","hash":"h1-f8552eb0"},
    "10c25261": {"text":"🏅 {name} is admitted among the masters.","hash":"h1-ef3e1d78"},
