    "4f010321": {"text":"Apprenticeship needed","hash":"h1-2f820039"},
    "4f17d265": {"text":"Horse Collar","hash":"h1-e9499af3"},
    "4f197757": {"text":"Bury the drowned man properly.","hash":"h1-6d839154"},
    "4f213a79": {"text":"Their current enterprise assignment will be preserved, or they will remain available only for manual assignment.","hash":"h1-38dc1947"},
    "4f23183d": {"text":"Utrecht","hash":"h1-9f55099e"},
    "4f24a491": {"text":"Moderation in all things.","hash":"h1-c166e862"},
    "4f289129": {"text":"Temporalities","hash":"h1-fc1d582d"},
    "4f400ef5": {"text":"A rare crown-restoration right reaches the usurper’s capital without a shared border. Pacts and defensive alliances forbid attacks. Your host musters when war begins — tap it, then a province to march (or let ⚙ automation command it). You may de-muster a raised host from the Deeds tab: the men preserved for your next muster depend on where it stands — all on your own land, half elsewhere in your realm, none abroad — and re-mustering waits out the same rearm window as a shattering.","hash":"h1-de9c324f"},
    "4f469b35": {"text":"An alliance envoy requires {money:25} in gifts.","hash":"h1-8d129c86"},
    "4f489d89": {"text":"Demand payment for the work you did.","hash":"h1-9812dfe7"},
    "4f4a9f31": {"text":"The hand-querns turn behind shuttered doors. The flour is poor, but it is yours.","hash":"h1-33f4d04d"},
    "4f4b3179": {"text":"Keep the ordinary stay and return journey. The Stay after marriage deed remains available until this journey ends.","hash":"h1-f9aefc97"},
    "4f4f2339": {"text":"Follows sovereign allegiance, not dynasty or county ownership","hash":"h1-b2f21a8f"},
    "4f53e8a1": {"text":"End the war now with a smaller prestige loss than abandoning it unilaterally.","hash":"h1-5b44a855"},
    "4f58464d": {"text":"War with {enemy}. The host musters at your banner even now — farmers, spears, and pride. Will you swell its ranks before it marches? And mark this: {target} falls only to a siege — your host must stand upon its walls while the council presses the works.","hash":"h1-213b9478"},
    "4f598bb3": {"text":"{name} · Standing {standing} · {progress} · paused—target is in {province}","hash":"h1-65d83822"},
    "4f59ad41": {"text":"You name the custom and the witnesses to it. The reeve scratches out the line, scowling.","hash":"h1-b1111829"},
    "4f5a7045": {"text":"Requires all: {technologies}.","hash":"h1-01758d5a"},
    "4f5d35b9": {"text":"overland army movement speed","hash":"h1-79c7f3ff"},
    "4f6220c9": {"text":"Search this list","hash":"h1-532aa04d"},
    "4f67f041": {"text":"Teach them yourself","hash":"h1-0eea93a9"},
    "4f7259fd": {"text":"Morgannwg","hash":"h1-7e89e8af"},
    "4f751b31": {"text":"Go the long way round.","hash":"h1-54c79411"},
    "4f8a2fe9": {"text":"Woodcutter’s son","hash":"h1-53a4698b"},
    "4f8fb5c1": {"text":"A hayloft is no fortress if the reeve knows his business.","hash":"h1-251b4a29"},
