    "7805b219": {"text":"By the fire, when the day’s work is done, the thought comes unbidden: a life is short, but a house endures. The children who carry your name will inherit more than your goods — your standing, your grudges, your chronicle. What you begin, they will continue; what you become, they will remember.","hash":"h1-a96b34d5"},
