    "a975716b": {"text":"There is a young man of the next quarter — quick to laugh, quicker to blush — and you had half a mind to make him yours. But the war has swallowed the season: the amir’s men are calling up every unwed youth who can level a spear, and this morning he stands in the muster with a borrowed shield on his arm and no notion that you exist. By dusk the column will be a smudge of dust on the war-road, and him with it. A woman does not ride with an army, they say — but they have not read the old tales as closely as you have.","hash":"h1-4552dd56"},
    "a975970d": {"text":"You mistake a proud old lord for a petitioner and compound it with a joke. A few smiles, poorly hidden.","hash":"h1-0a96f0e0"},
