    "c7f7963d": {"text":"are global two-camp campaigns called by an active Pope or Caliph after their historical unlock. Freeholders and greater ranks may answer during the 180-day gathering, promise one to three years of service, and name a hoped-for crown, sacred custody, exact duchy or county, beneficiary, or honor. Sovereigns field their own host, while vassals and unlanded volunteers serve through expedition events. Attackers must occupy the sacred places, at least half the target counties, and 60% of its development before the eight-year deadline. After an attacker victory, a settlement council weighs contribution beside the vow, occupation, rights, local support, and religious standing before any land changes hands.","hash":"h1-c0dc261e"},
