    "eb074661": {"text":"You are {name}, a spear in the service of the lord of {province}. Wages are thin, but battlefields are where nobodies become somebodies.","hash":"h1-b85a5380"},
    "eb0e7755": {"text":"Mud lanes, low roofs, and every face turning to mark the newcomer. {settlement} is small enough that nothing here goes unnoticed — including you.","hash":"h1-ada11036"},
    "eb173131": {"text":"You have chosen your moment and rehearsed your words; today you mean to ask {suitor} for a life together. But the war reaches your door first. Even as you square your shoulders to speak, the chief’s men are working down the lane — and {suitor}’s name is among those called, every unwed lad who can hold a spear. There will be no answer today: only a borrowed shield thrust into his arms, and dust on the war-road by dusk.","hash":"h1-cef4d326"},
    "eb1a7309": {"text":"Carry your suit to a higher lord: escape a harsh liege, or rise under a greater one.","hash":"h1-57158a5d"},
